<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44593" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔοδ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>easy to pass</i>, of
			mountains, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				4.8.10
			</span></i>; of a road, <i>easy to travel</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁδὸς . . εὐοδωτάτη τοῖς ὑποζυγίοις</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				4.2.9
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ εὔοδα ἔσται ὑμῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Nu.</u>
					14.41
				</span></i>
			. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όδως</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, πορεύεσθαι</span> ib. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pr.</u>
				24.64
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				30.29
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i>free from difficulty, simple</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Alm.</u>
				1.2
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			). Adv.
			<i>simply, readily</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>D.</u>
					3.11
				</span></i>
			: 
				Sup.
			 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ώτατα</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, τῷ τῆς ἀνδρείας ὀνόματι προσαγορεύεσθαι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				81
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>favourable</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τι</span>
			Mnesith. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				3.92c
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ εὔοδος θεός</span>, of Pan, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				4705b
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				38
			</span></i> (Egypt, <span class="entity">iii B. C.</span>), al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
				826
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
